 host that created the checkpoint","session_id?":"string, exact host-provided session identifier (pair with agent)","agent?":"string, agent harness identifier such as tau or claude-code or codex","tau_session_id?":"string, legacy Tau session identifier (read compatibility only)","claude_session_id?":"string, legacy Claude Code session identifier (read compatibility only)","codex_session_id?":"string, legacy Codex session identifier (read compatibility only)","codex_turn_id?":"string, Codex turn identifier","trigger?":"string, compaction trigger or deliberate checkpoint source","model?":"string, active model slug when known","capture?(enum, how this checkpoint was produced)":["extractive","deliberate","summarized"]}}},"content":"# Coding Session\n\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n\nExamples:\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":29707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2007},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b2a97c-b7b5-4fd4-8757-b92f993bd6ae","uuid":"ef930ce3-b686-4947-a2fb-5b8596032180","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:15:48.479Z","request_id":"req_011CgfpXPCYEG3xrLEEjnG2a","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019dsW6ia3pxCmUiWVauD2Z6","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019dsW6ia3pxCmUiWVauD2Z6","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\\ntitle: Coding Session\\npermalink: ms/schemas/coding-session\\nchecksum: d5af58c0bb0f98ac803bd4309efeb0260473421708dc705deacdfa9a54f9ff03\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b2a97c-b7b5-4fd4-8757-b92f993bd6ae","uuid":"d502a16a-5348-476f-8411-930bca827df5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:15:49.956Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\\ntitle: Coding Session\\npermalink: ms/schemas/coding-session\\nchecksum: d5af58c0bb0f98ac803bd4309efeb0260473421708dc705deacdfa9a54f9ff03\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\ntitle: Coding Session\npermalink: ms/schemas/coding-session\nchecksum: d5af58c0bb0f98ac803bd4309efeb0260473421708dc705deacdfa9a54f9ff03"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019dsW6ia3pxCmUiWVauD2Z6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfpXPLDfdrb13pYAaHUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VNLd7o5GV9WyodLN5CuK1F","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"ms","directory":"schemas","note_type":"schema","title":"Decision","metadata":{"entity":"Decision","version":1,"schema":{"decision":"string, the choice that was made","rationale?":"string, why this choice over the alternatives","alternative?(array)":"string, options that were considered and not taken","consequence?(array)":"string, what this decision commits us to","context?":"string, the situation that prompted the decision","affects?(array)":"Entity, work or notes this decision bears on","supersedes?":"Entity, a prior decision this one replaces"},"settings":{"validation":"warn","frontmatter":{"status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision)":["open","accepted","superseded","rejected"],"decided?":"string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)","project?":"string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to"}}},"content":"# Decision\n\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\n\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n\n## Frontmatter\n\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\nnever blocking.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":29707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2007},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b2a97c-b7b5-4fd4-8757-b92f993bd6ae","uuid":"b4bf72e3-2dd6-4a81-b255-56798709c8cd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:15:51.742Z","request_id":"req_011CgfpXPCYEG3xrLEEjnG2a","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VNLd7o5GV9WyodLN5CuK1F","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VNLd7o5GV9WyodLN5CuK1F","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Decision.md\\ntitle: Decision\\npermalink: ms/schemas/decision\\nchecksum: b39f2896104eec2c9f72f0b5bd63e58feb5584678ddcfc18c84c61c7eeb21ca2\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b2a97c-b7b5-4fd4-8757-b92f993bd6ae","uuid":"58080620-23a9-4e25-8321-edf08227535c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:15:52.016Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Decision.md\\ntitle: Decision\\npermalink: ms/schemas/decision\\nchecksum: b39f2896104eec2c9f72f0b5bd63e58feb5584678ddcfc18c84c61c7eeb21ca2\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Decision.md\ntitle: Decision\npermalink: ms/schemas/decision\nchecksum: b39f2896104eec2c9f72f0b5bd63e58feb5584678ddcfc18c84c61c7eeb21ca2"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VNLd7o5GV9WyodLN5CuK1F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfpXPLDfdrb13pYAaHUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C9Cjzq7qdToZ3tEVAP8NNJ","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"ms","directory":"schemas","note_type":"schema","title":"Task","metadata":{"entity":"Task","version":1,"schema":{"description":"string, what needs to be done","status?(enum, current state)":["active","blocked","done","abandoned"],"assigned_to?":"string, who is working on this","steps?(array)":"string, ordered steps to complete","current_step?":"integer, which step number we're on (1-indexed)","context?":"string, key context needed to resume after memory loss","started?":"string, when work began","completed?":"string, when work finished","blockers?(array)":"string, what's preventing progress","parent_task?":"Task, parent task if this is a subtask"},"settings":{"validation":"warn"}},"content":"# Task\n\nA **Task** is work-in-progress tracked as a note, so it survives context\ncompaction and shows up in the next session's brief. This schema matches the\nframework-agnostic `memory-tasks` skill. For the full task workflow, use that skill.\n\nTasks are found by the SessionStart hook via structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"task\", \"status\": \"active\"})`.\n\n## Frontmatter vs observations\n\nPut queryable fields (`status`, `priority`, `current_step`) in frontmatter so\n`filters` can find them, and mirror them as `- [status] active`\nobservations so `bm_schema(command=\"validate\")` sees them. `note_type=\"Task\"` is stored as\nlowercase `task` in frontmatter, so search with `note_types=[\"task\"]`.\nValidation is `warn` — advisory, never blocking.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":29707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2007},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6b2a97c-b7b5-4fd4-8757-b92f993bd6ae","uuid":"56c90dde-8430-438d-a89c-1a120a2d48d4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T10:15:54.676Z","request_id":"req_011CgfpXPCYEG3xrLEEjnG2a","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01C9Cjzq7qdToZ3tEVAP8NNJ","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
